    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d93-a3">

                <pb facs="0187" n="107" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg107"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Dr. Magalhaes to Mr. Bryan.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ministry of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Rio
                                de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-07-09"><hi rendition="#italic">July 9,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>I have received the two notes which Mr. Charles Page Bryan, envoy extraordinary
                    and minister plenipotentiary of the United States of America, addressed to me on
                    the 27th of May and the 28th of June, requesting, at the desire of the Cuban
                    Government, permission for the consular officers of the United States to
                    exercise provisionally their good offices in behalf of that Republic and its
                    citizens; and informing me that the military occupation of the island by the
                    American Government ceased on the 20th of the month just past (May), an
                    independent and republican government having been organized under the presidency
                    of Señor Estrada Palma.</p>
                <p>The Government of Cuba has not yet communicated to that of Brazil the important
                    events referred to by Mr. Bryan, and that Government has therefore not been
                    recognized in the usual form, but the President of the Republic, assured that
                    this action will not be delayed, gives with pleasure the permission
                    requested.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Olyntho de
                    Magalhaes.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
